<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU gives Spain 115 mn euros aid over Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee0e2ee7c85af5dc09b0b403eb5589e60f382346106b5168b4833d3347533a54</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:06:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis--38a16ccc97da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">The EU on Wednesday said it was granting Spain 115 million euros ($130 million) in emergency aid to help bolster border security and assist returns after the massive migrant rush into the north African exclave. More than 70,000 migrants crossed into Spanish territory from Morocco on July 30 and 31 in an unprecedented rush that left scores dead, most by drowning as they tried to swim around a breakwater. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rungis market chief on supply chains and feeding the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24924d92dee35f152a4c28ea6bdd9c8cf23ab22ff1a7b0ad122abcea4778abb5</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:05:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world--b449a157d7e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world" /><summary type="html">In today’s edition, FRANCE 24’s Delano D'Souza speaks with the man at the heart of France's food supply chain. Stéphane Layani is the head of the Rungis wholesale food market – the largest of its kind in Europe – and chairman of the World Union of Wholesale Markets. Earlier this year Layani came out with a book titled Le Monde a faim, or "The World is Hungry" in English. In his interview, he gives his perspective on how France's food system will transform in the coming years.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic calls snap elections after nearly two years of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:131e1dba88cd207dd3df59bc8b07c5075916af63e02dc9354984f871a6b9b9f2</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:15:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests--5f70b882a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic on Wednesday called snap parliamentary elections for October 25. They are expected to be a key test of his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strike near Ukraine-Moldova border kills at least two as Ukraine targets oil terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f22ea4d2c5c03f136a6cee9ed5d87df1ed5cdeef2773e875177b43e08b54d8</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:51:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-ter--fc9e4da4f8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-terminal" /><summary type="html">An overnight Russian drone strike at a border crossing between Ukraine and Moldova killed at least two people, Odesa's regional governor said Wednesday. Moldovan Prime Minister Vasile Tofan said that 17 drones had hit Moldovan territory in August alone as both Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on military and energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Travellers in UK face ongoing disruption after air traffic control glitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea87a311684be06e5847f22d8c7d77e73df4354b0481dfb360dfb37dde22f06e</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T03:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch--92d15f16fe8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch" /><summary type="html">Flights from British airports began to resume Wednesday after a glitch in the country's air traffic control service left hundreds of thousands of passengers stranded and 2,000 cancellations, costing airlines millions of pounds. Authorities warned that travellers would continue to experience delays as airlines scrambled to recover from the outage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump tells Putin he wants swift end to Ukraine war, Kremlin says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5482155f45e4756fa3f9f910356a4e6c8abfb54489ed50fd9279135745862d8</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:07:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says--5f2aae4d01c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told Russian President Vladimir Putin he wanted a swift end to the Ukraine war, the Kremlin said, arguing that peace could pave the way for a broad restoration of US-Russia ties. The hour-long call Tuesday followed weekend talks by US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Moscow and Kyiv to try to revive stalled peace efforts.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Missiles or mediation? Trump envoys shuttle between Russia and Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ff7f8fd047f69f7506923c7bbf86ed43ff86b8a15634b83b0803399c715550f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine--b5fc503da412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s momentum on the battlefield was a primary focus at July’s NATO summit in Turkey. Kyiv’s long-range drones and US President Donald Trump’s surprise announcement that the Washington would allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles on in the country. However, Trump's deal has yet to materialize. Moreover, Russia has ramped up cruise missile launches and Ukraine has run out of air defenses to stop them. Moscow is also failing to stop incoming missiles. In today’s edition we ask: What happens in war when offense proves better than defense for both sides?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cbfcaefa8594cdfb9af054c6a563a44f8fc960ee05cc2ca3c441709cb494b3e</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower reopens after row over limits on women staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1b2dd5b015f4fba0c96454c364ec33b721429364f72ff8e942560ef1e17d4a5</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:18:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff--477be6cb13b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff" /><summary type="html">The Eiffel Tower reopened Tuesday, a day after one of the world's most-visited landmarks was closed by a strike to protest what a union official called "unacceptable" management instructions limiting the presence of women during a visit by a Hindu religious group close to Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s ruling nationalist party.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spoiler alert: AI in cinema 'just a tool, won’t replace actors and human beings'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a57f00a31016f62765a1deca732af6ee53bc69314493c660b39d64348c61b4f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:11:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1--59df42aa2e9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome film producer Lahoucine Grimich. He challenges the prevailing narrative that cinema is an industry in existential crisis. While acknowledging that viewing habits have dramatically shifted since the pandemic, he argues that streaming platforms, public support and theatrical exhibition are not competing forces. As demonstrated in the French model, they form parts of an interconnected financing ecosystem in which cinema can adapt without ever abandoning the big screen. He frames filmmaking as a form of cultural sovereignty: societies need films not simply as entertainment, but to recognise themselves and to create what he calls “new imaginaries.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Kyiv, ending three-day halt for US talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3c6e28a6b316dc82a54e702e8af63ec52bb1b9f97564efc00ae3d95504aa4a</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:35:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-ending-three-day-halt-for-us-talks--d105618bccd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-ending-three-day-halt-for-us-talks" /><summary type="html">Russian missiles and drones pounded Kyiv overnight, killing two people and sending smoke billowing above the Ukrainian capital, ending Moscow's temporary halt to strikes on the city.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Ukraine, teens try to heal from trauma of war at summer camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a357ea5d31106d2c8db87588d188b9cc280c4350d5f5a0fb4ab7d1b4ec7f809</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:10:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260908-in-ukraine-teens-try-to-heal-from-trauma-of-war-at-summer-camp--b5b19daa74ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260908-in-ukraine-teens-try-to-heal-from-trauma-of-war-at-summer-camp" /><summary type="html">The psychological impact on the Ukrainian population of nearly five years of full-scale Russian onslaught is hard to overstate. Children and teenagers are particularly at risk of trauma. With support from foreign philanthropists, one Ukrainian NGO is trying to help at least a few teenagers cope better, via summer camps that mix therapy and fun. Our correspondent Gulliver Cragg reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>French police hunt Renoir thieves after lightning museum heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555aa922675459fefb12c03ce5e96e2c0f2346b7818f86eb5c8a1c30918d1197</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T08:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-thieves-steal-works-of-art-worth-9-million-euros-from-france-s-renoir-museum--54621680077e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-thieves-steal-works-of-art-worth-9-million-euros-from-france-s-renoir-museum" /><summary type="html">Two thieves climbed through a window and stole four valuable Renoir paintings on Tuesday from the Renoir Museum in the town of Cagnes-sur-Mer on the French Riviera, but abandoned two of the artworks as they fled, authorities said. Investigators have launched a national search for the perpetrators.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French AI startup Mistral valued at over 21 billion euros after latest funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab36a37694e144d3c0d63cef44a7b988d27a15d42afb22d2221a2e17c53911db</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:03:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-french-ai-startup-mistral-raises-3-billion-euros-after-latest-funding--93b791671133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-french-ai-startup-mistral-raises-3-billion-euros-after-latest-funding" /><summary type="html">French AI company Mistral announced Tuesday that it had raised three billion euros ($3.5 billion) in what it described as the largest-ever European tech fundraising, valuing the startup at over 21 billion euros. While still an upstart compared to the AI giants OpenAI or Anthropic, Mistral says it is carving a niche by offering models that companies can run themselves with their own data.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin tells Trump that Russia has no 'aggressive plans' towards Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe35448d8c8cc82305f4beab785f9ca1fef962ac6218a1ed02d1796fc5a026c6</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:00:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt--c216aa8a2eec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and his counterpart Donald Trump held a “constructive” phone call Tuesday during which the Russian leader emphasised that Moscow had “no aggressive plans towards Europe”, the Kremlin said. The call followed a visit to Moscow by US envoys for talks at ending the war in Ukraine. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU says no place for 'glorification of war criminals' as Mladic buried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2962da943164fdf754d383cbf2d7e292866a417a3c24558ca17fad42102eb946</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T21:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried--c505261200fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Monday denounced any "glorification" of convicted war criminal Ratko Mladic in Serbia, as thousands gathered in Belgrade for his funeral. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Only the beginning? German far right's breakthrough shakes Europe to its core</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:687ebf409debbaae8d899780ce13e0724d49e9df0ae57564afa75f846c6a7b5f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T19:38:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core--984465a67934.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core" /><summary type="html">The result was not enough to win outright, but certainly enough to shake Germany and Europe to their core: the far-right Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) trounced the ruling conservatives in the impoverished former East German state of Saxony-Anhalt in Sunday's election. We ask about the consequences of voting for an anti-immigrant, pro-Russian party that wants schools to teach less about the ills of Hitler and more about the glory of Bismarck.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'What we see right now is that Putin has zero interest in ending the war', Ukrainian MP Yasko says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc3fdd634b2abd2e79b1a59b31241e4567485b33bbc28b5343a614f39c88b3b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:38:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says--3db6e994afb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff on Monday touted progress in weekend discussions with Ukraine and Russia, raising the prospect of reviving three-way peace talks to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II. Ukrainian MP Lisa Yasko says that "we don't trust these talks", describing the US envoys' flattery towards Russian President Vladimir Putin as "disgraceful".</summary></entry><entry><title>Avalanche kills at least 11 climbers in southern Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89330cbc6455ebfbd506518d4dfcbf6e510f4a9b6ff6ce126b2156639a3e1b08</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:00:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia--cc82d0868712.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia" /><summary type="html">⁠At least ​11 people were killed and six ​others injured after an avalanche struck a group of climbers in Russia's ​southern Kabardino-Balkaria ‌Republic, local emergency services said. The ‌avalanche swept down Mount Mizhirgi, ⁠one of the highest peaks in Russia's North Caucasus.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1d32ecce8d2d57fab5a5f5dad1c1bdcea59ce189e78700cf085b45060252fb1</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1--3d84be7d1802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75eb937a1f1117856993f7fdd435e4acadcc86ab7a246882d0a037d55b75e48c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd--3acc1083cc66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd" /><summary type="html">Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa12b7441f4df1b59bb3a7d4739682df6eaaa5e39b86f524c1d3a431cc7488d0</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1--355f2ad6ae17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37c4359633fbee2c6ef5e3634c5bc41b9b8399d6b5b7447acda675e7c3d9db13</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:05:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election--1210a591a6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6860c4a98adcbb3563404bce6bee2667f7bc91c5c480941a80225d1987e6734c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:14:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court--eec11aeeb4e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court" /><summary type="html">Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of mourners gather in Belgrade for war criminal Mladic's funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61c59f63fe9f4797cb9cfb8022866c51eb0edf6f04b05a2edd89355109485c1b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral--0ff58bef6eca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral" /><summary type="html">Thousands of mourners on Monday gathered at a church in Belgrade for the funeral of Ratko Mladic, who died in The Hague, Netherlands, on August 27 while serving a life sentence for genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity. The European Union heavily criticised the decision to hold a public funeral service with Marta Kos, the bloc's enlargement commissioner, having cancelled an upcoming visit to Serbia in protest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Merz 'deeply shocked' by far-right AfD's historic electoral victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cb636323073432f074b21b0033bcb42cdba4836a4aedb2971ef0f9c0bdf7d58</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T06:30:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory--3bd65a3dc7ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz told the press on Monday that he was "deeply shocked" by the far-right AfD's historic victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election a day earlier. The AfD is labelled a "right-wing extremist" group by Germany's domestic intelligence agency, and some of its staff are former members of a since-banned neo-Nazi organisation. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz vows to stick with reforms despite election drubbing by far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51443c546e12a7c49342a36a6a572056c2ed876228cd0568e883f31c8ffbbfe0</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T05:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course--601c526382cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday vowed to press ahead with his reform agenda despite a blistering election defeat for his centre-right CDU in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right AfD won almost 44 percent of the vote. Merz called the result his party’s worst defeat in decades.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys bring ‘more effective’ Ukraine peace proposals to Kyiv, official says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8270d94f6332a3d7af07c5ad6f559b0ff2b14d34437f4447cc846e513fd898fb</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv--37419914ba3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv" /><summary type="html">US envoys brought new, “more effective” proposals to Kyiv aimed at ending the war with Russia, a senior Ukrainian presidential official said on Sunday. President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner described talks positively but announced no breakthrough, as Zelensky warned fighting could continue into winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU to boost Greenland investment amid Trump annexation claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5633faefd886062bd1cfd7cc35fd0f5c72e960eaf6079579b9d5bffce3525c1a</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation--2b5a527b0c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is expected to announce increased EU investment in Greenland on Monday, including in critical minerals, satellite communications and renewable energy. Her two-day visit signals support for Greenland and Denmark amid US President Donald Trump’s push for American control of the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Ready to talk': German far right celebrates victory in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8984badb6b30e39499d035c941fb5c2744e47203f8cc34be34eca50736d4ee64</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T17:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory--e252fd4fc28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory" /><summary type="html">"Everything is possible" was the campaign slogan of the Alternative for Germany (AfD) in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right party has won a landslide election victory, although they appear short of a majority in the state parliament. Ulrich Siegmund, who is in pole position to become the state leader, knows he has history in his grasp. We get reaction from CSU MP Tobias Winkler.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry></feed>
